[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi, I am interested in formalising circuit complexity theory in Lean and contributing to CSLib. I am doing a Bachelor's project under Prof Balagopal Komarath, a complexity theory researcher at my college (IIT Gandhinagar), on this subject. </p>\n<p>I am thinking of formalising a lemma from Heribert Vollmer's Introduction to Circuit Complexity that relates bounded-width branching programs to M-programs over finite Monoids.<br>\nThe exact statement given in Vollmer is the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">*.</span>\n<span class=\"n\">There</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">family</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bounded</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">width</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">branching</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">programs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">polynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span>\n<span class=\"n\">that</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">computes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">c_A</span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span>\n<span class=\"n\">there</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">an</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">program</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">polynomial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">such</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">that</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I would like to know whether this would be a good contribution to CSLib. I would especially appreciate <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"448405\">@Alex Meiburg</span>'s view on whether this would be a good addition to his work at CircuitComp.</p>",
        "id": 572560606,
        "sender_full_name": "Anvit Aggarwal",
        "timestamp": 1770491825
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This would be very appropriate and I would appreciate it. :) My repo has a definition of monoid programs (I called them <code>BarringtonProgram</code>, which is another name I've seen in the literature), and I have the conversion from a <code>BarringtonProgram</code> to <code>LayeredBranchingProgram</code> as it works for symmetric groups (which gives a smaller width than the obvious construction for other monoids).</p>\n<p>The statement you wrote is slightly stronger, because you allow different (I assume) accepting sets <code>F</code>. So this would be a good stronger thing to have. </p>\n<p>The other direction (forward of your implication), that a bounded-width branching program can be converted back to a monoid program, could go \"directly\" or via the NC0 compilation, which is something I've been looking at doing a bit. I think it would be good.</p>",
        "id": 572578549,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1770512109
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The reverse direction, I think, can be stated in an appropriately general way that gets you the width-5 necessary for Barrington's theorem while also getting you your statement for any arbitrary monoid.</p>\n<p>If you have a monoid M with a faithful action on a set S, and then accepting set F of S, then you can get a branching program of width |S|. So for any monoid you can have its own action on itself, for a branching program of width |M|. For the symmetric group S_n, it acts on Fin n, so you get a branching program of width n.</p>",
        "id": 572578732,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1770512381
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This doesn't actually require it to be a monoid at all then.</p>",
        "id": 572578790,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1770512449
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi,</p>\n<p>I’m trying to construct a layered branching program from a monoid program via the monoid acting on itself.<br>\nIn the current definition of LayeredBranchingProgram:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LayeredBranchingProgram</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The node type and the branching alphabet β are both required to live in the same universe (Type v). <br>\nHowever, nodes are elements of a monoid γ : Type v, and β is the input alphabet (e.g., Fin 2 : Type 0). <br>\nBecause of this, Lean forces me to lift β (using ULift), but because of this, I have to use ULift everywhere, and in some cases, it causes issues like the following:</p>\n<p>BPF.computes A<br>\n  -- where A : FuncFamily₁ (Fin 2)<br>\n  -- but BPF expects FuncFamily₁ (ULift (Fin 2))</p>\n<p>Is there a reason for requiring β and nodes to live in the same universe in this definition? Or would it be better to change the universe level of nodes?</p>\n<p>Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 581213874,
        "sender_full_name": "Anvit Aggarwal",
        "timestamp": 1774297712
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have trouble following entirely, but it sounds like you should just take v and w to be the same universe, in your application?</p>\n<p>If that doesn't make sense, maybe you can send along a snippet of the code you're trying to make work?</p>",
        "id": 581221478,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1774300695
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sorry, that wasn't clear enough.</p>\n<p>I am trying to obtain a Branching Program by a Monoid's Action on itself. In the original definition of toBranchingProgram, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05556em;\">γ</span></span></span></span> is of type Type; however, I have defined it as of Type v since <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05556em;\">γ</span></span></span></span> is a monoid. </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">toBranchingProgram'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidablePred</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">FaithfulSMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">LayeredBranchingProgram</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GP</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">len</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nodeVar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GP</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">var</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">edges</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">down</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GP</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">perm1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GP</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">perm0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dest</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">dest</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GP</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">perm1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GP</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">perm0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hk</span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u'</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">startUnique</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">up</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">uniq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">up</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eq_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">retVals</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GP</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">len</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>According to the definition of LayeredBranchingProgram, <code>nodes (n: Fin (depth + 1))</code> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\beta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05278em;\">β</span></span></span></span> have the same universe level. Because of this, I have defined <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\beta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05278em;\">β</span></span></span></span> as <code>ULift.{v, 0} (Fin 2)</code>. I want to use this construction in the proof of the following lemma:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exists_boundedWidthBP_poly_iff_exists_monoidProgram</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FuncFamily₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BPF</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BPFamily</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BPF</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">BPF</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">computes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BPF</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hasWidth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">BPF</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hasSize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">poly</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">PF</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProgramFamily</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">PF</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hasLength</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">poly</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PF</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">recognizes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here, A is expected to be of Type <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FuncFamily</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\text{FuncFamily}_1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9386em;vertical-align:-0.2441em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">FuncFamily</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.207em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4559em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2441em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (ULift.{v, 0} (Fin 2)) but is of type <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>FuncFamily</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\text{FuncFamily}_1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9386em;vertical-align:-0.2441em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">FuncFamily</span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.207em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4559em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2441em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (Fin 2). </p>\n<p>But, if I change A's type, then I need to change other definitions, such as <code>GroupProgram.eval</code>. I think that this is because of having the same universe levels for <code>nodes (n: Fin (depth + 1))</code> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\beta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05278em;\">β</span></span></span></span>. Do you think that is necessary, or could it be changed?</p>",
        "id": 581293491,
        "sender_full_name": "Anvit Aggarwal",
        "timestamp": 1774337853
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that my message was probably not clear, still. What I meant to ask is whether in the LayeredBranchingProgram definition, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\beta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05278em;\">β</span></span></span></span> and <code>nodes n</code>need to be in the same universe level (Type v). I think that this constraint may not be required.</p>",
        "id": 582018439,
        "sender_full_name": "Anvit Aggarwal",
        "timestamp": 1774551877
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Would it be safe to instead allow:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>β : Type v</code></li>\n<li><code>nodes (n : Fin (depth + 1)) : Type w</code> (separate universe)?</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 582021013,
        "sender_full_name": "Anvit Aggarwal",
        "timestamp": 1774552814
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You are setting yourself up for pain when you compose circuits</p>",
        "id": 582036538,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1774558537
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Basically you have to cast all the nodes arguments to a larger fin type</p>",
        "id": 582036611,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1774558558
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I understand that but my issue is about universe levels, specifically in the definition of <code>LayeredBranchingPrograms</code>. Currently, it is defined as the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LayeredBranchingProgram</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">nodeVar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">castSucc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">edges</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">castSucc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">succ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">startUnique</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unique</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">retVals</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">last</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">γ</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Notice that <code>nodes n</code> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\beta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.05278em;\">β</span></span></span></span> (which represents the input alphabet) have the same universe level (v). I think that this constraint might not be required.</p>",
        "id": 582083416,
        "sender_full_name": "Anvit Aggarwal",
        "timestamp": 1774587154
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think that different universe levels could be used for the two.</p>",
        "id": 582083605,
        "sender_full_name": "Anvit Aggarwal",
        "timestamp": 1774587357
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"466334\">@Shreyas Srinivas</span>, I might not have fully understood what you said. What I understood is that when composing two <code>LayeredBranchingProgram</code>s (say, A and B), we need to cast an index<br>\n<code>i : Fin (A.depth + B.depth + 1)</code> into either <code>Fin (A.depth + 1)</code> or <code>Fin (B.depth + 1)</code>, which requires proof. For example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">depth</span>\n<span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">depth</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is this what you meant? Also, is this related to the requirement that <code>nodes</code> and <code>β</code> live in the same universe?</p>",
        "id": 582432449,
        "sender_full_name": "Anvit Aggarwal",
        "timestamp": 1774810504
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes. And also the other way around.</p>",
        "id": 582432727,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1774810781
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You’ll run into a lot of arithmetic headaches</p>",
        "id": 582432741,
        "sender_full_name": "Shreyas Srinivas",
        "timestamp": 1774810791
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think you are better off defining your layered branching program inductively instead of using functions from Fin like this. Then all definitions can rely on peeling off the constructors and you will reduce a lot of casts</p>",
        "id": 582446746,
        "sender_full_name": "Quang Dao",
        "timestamp": 1774824002
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>A lesson I learned from developing ArkLib (not very relevant, but just for context)</p>",
